      "id": "techcrunch-2026-08-26-apple-is-holding-its-iphone-launch-event-on-september-9",
      "title": "Apple is holding its iPhone launch event on September 9",
      "summary": "The event is expected to be a notable one, as Apple is rumored to unveil its long-awaited foldable iPhone. It'll also be the first Apple event with John Ternus as CEO, who is scheduled to take the reins of the tech giant from Tim Cook on September 1.",
      "body": "Apple announced on Wednesday that its next launch event is taking place on September 9, with a “Surprise and Shine” tagline.\nThe event is expected to be a notable one, as Apple is rumored to unveil its long-awaited foldable iPhone. It’ll also be the first Apple event with John Ternus as CEO. Ternus is scheduled to take the reins of the tech giant from Tim Cook on September 1.\nApple is expected to announce the new iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max, but the two models are rumored to be relatively iterative upgrades rather than a major redesign. Reports have indicated that the company won’t be announcing the standard iPhone 18 until next year.\nThe tech giant is also expected to introduce the Apple Watch Series 12 and Apple Watch Ultra, alongside new smart home devices.\nIn addition to the new hardware, the company may announce launch dates for iOS 27, iPadOS 27, macOS Golden Gate, and other upcoming software updates.\nThe event will take place at the Apple Park Campus in Cupertino, California at 10 am PT.",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Aisha Malik",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-26T16:53:07.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-26-at-12.45.18-PM.png?resize=1200,927",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/26/apple-is-holding-its-iphone-launch-event-on-september-9/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-08-26-portrait-of-ann-widdecombe-put-up-in-parliament-for-mps-retu",
      "title": "Portrait of Ann Widdecombe put up in Parliament for MPs' return",
      "summary": "The framed photograph forms part of work by MPs to install a permament memorial for the former minister.",
      "body": "A portrait of Ann Widdecombe has been erected in Parliament to remember the former MP, who was found dead with serious head injuries last month.The picture of the ex-Conservative minister was put up on Tuesday in Portcullis House, where many MPs' offices are located, in time for the return from summer recess next week.It forms part of ongoing talks about a fitting memorial for the minister turned Reform UK spokeswoman, who died aged 78 after being found in her Devon home. Joshua Kerry, 28, has been charged with murder.Helen Grant, Widdecombe's successor as MP for the area of Maidstone in Kent, said the portrait was \"the start of a lasting tribute to Ann\".\"I am delighted that the Speaker of the House of Commons has confirmed that this portrait of Ann Widdecombe will be on show in Parliament, following her tragic death earlier this year,\" Grant said. Work is underway \"to explore a more permanent commemoration on the Parliamentary estate\", she added.The chosen photograph was taken in 2010 in the Cloister Corridor of the Palace of Westminster.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
