    {
      "id": "theverge-2026-08-26-rockstar-finally-responds-to-8216-heartbreaking-8217-gta-6-l",
      "title": "Rockstar finally responds to &#8216;heartbreaking&#8217; GTA 6 leaks",
      "summary": "Rockstar Games has released its first official statement following days of sustained leaks of footage from Grand Theft Auto VI, calling the period \"heartbreaking for our team.\"\n\"It would be an understatement to say that having videos of Grand Theft Auto VI gameplay leak in this way has been heartbreaking for our team, and this is obviously not how we intended for you to see the game after all this",
      "body": "Rockstar Games has released its first official statement following days of sustained leaks of footage from Grand Theft Auto VI, calling the period “heartbreaking for our team.”\n“It would be an understatement to say that having videos of Grand Theft Auto VI gameplay leak in this way has been heartbreaking for our team, and this is obviously not how we intended for you to see the game after all this time,” the studio said in a statement published today on social media. “We are very sorry that everything has taken as long as it has —&nbsp;from getting the game finished (nearly there!) to sharing more details and official gameplay, and providing the community with everything you want to know.”\nFootage from the game has been repeatedly shared in recent days from an apparently playable build of the game. A person or organization calling themself “CyberLeek” has claimed responsibility for the leaks, which have been used in part to promote a cryptocurrency. Publisher Take-Two Interactive has requested to be able to subpoena Microsoft and Discord over the copyright-infringing content in the hope of identifying the source of the leaks.\nTomorrow fans are getting an “extended look” at the game in a show that will stream exclusively on Netflix at 3PM ET. The long-awaited game itself will release on November 19th.\n> We know that many of you have been waiting to hear from us regarding the events of the past week. It would be an understatement to say that having videos of Grand Theft Auto VI gameplay leak in this way has been heartbreaking for our team, and this is obviously not how we intended for you to see the game after all this time. We are very sorry that everything has taken as long as it has - from getting the game finished (nearly there!) to sharing more details and official gameplay, and providing the community with everything you want to know.\n> We are very excited for everyone to see the extended look tomorrow. It has taken longer than we wanted to get it ready, but as with everything we do, we know we need to exceed your expectations, and we are determined to deliver at the level you expect and deserve. While it is unfortunate that the intended game experience may now be impacted by some spoilers, we hope that everyone will wait a bit longer to experience the game for themselves on November 19.\n> We want to thank everyone in the community who has reached out with messages of support this past week - your words have meant more to this team than you can imagine. Ultimately, we are making this game for you, and without you, we would not have the privilege of making games.\n> We look forward to sharing more with you soon.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Gaming",
        "News",
        "Security",
        "Tech"
      ],
      "author": "Dominic Preston",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-26T12:04:15.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/06/ULTIMATE_EDITION_01_de9b57.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,3.4613147178592,100,93.077370564282",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/games/984959/gta-vi-leaks-rockstar-games-official-statement-heartbreaking",
      "readTimeMinutes": 2,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-08-26-proliferate-yc-s25-is-hiring",
      "title": "Proliferate (YC S25) Is Hiring",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/proliferate/jobs/OgpCKYJ-founding-product-engineer\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49447480\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Proliferate is the open-source, self-hostable AI IDE where you can collaborate with agents as a team.\nLonger term, we are building the substrate through which companies deploy agents for real work. We believe the future of all work is companies staffed by thousands of agents and we’re building the platform that manages them.\nWe’re early, the product still has rough edges, and we’re oriented around large goals. We are backed by True Ventures, Pear VC, and 50+ YC founders- and we work together in person in SoMa, San Francisco.\nI’m Pablo! I finished my bachelor’s at 17, ran a consulting company at 18, completed my master’s in AI at 19, and joined Onyx (YC W24) as engineer #1. I spent a year building enterprise AI search before starting Proliferate.\nI started Proliferate because I believe this is the most ambitious thing I could possibly be working on, and I’ve turned down eight figures in acquisition offers to keep building it.\nWe are hiring exceptional founding engineers. You will be one of the first engineers at Proliferate, working side by side with the founder and early team, and owning major parts of the product end to end.\nYou might, one week to the next:\nDesign a new interface for human-agent collaboration made possible by a model capability that landed a few days ago.\nTurn repeated engineering or company processes into fully agent-owned workflows.\nTake a sharp customer pain point from rough idea to polished product surface in days.\nWe ship unusually fast. A tiny team means your decisions immediately change the product.\nWe reason from first principles, protect long stretches of deep work, and use agents liberally but intentionally through the company.\nWe are deeply AGI-pilled, ship fast and dream big, but we don’t confuse recklessness with speed or grandiosity with ambition.\nWe care about what works and what impacts people’s lives.\nWe are intentional about our long term health and consider performance core to the company culture- we work according to the following.\nFree gym (Equinox or comparable gym)\nFree meals at the office (be warned- we tend to eat a lot of Sweetgreen)\nMornings are protected deep work time- company policy of no meetings if we can avoid them\nYou might be a great fit if\nYou have shipped something 0→1. Ex-founders are especially welcome!\nYou use AI tools seriously and have real opinions about where they fail\nYou want unusually dense learning and ownership\nYou are looking for the most ambitious project you can find and want your work to matter immediately\n30-minute technical conversation with a codebase and agents open on your end\nPaid work trial: 1-3 days, $1-3K",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "pablo24602",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-26T12:00:07.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/logos/8a51b468ded81d8f8847dd75ed281beeb0a71b77.png?1771376897",
