      "id": "hackernews-2026-08-25-clara-yc-p26-is-hiring-a-growth-engineer-to-bring-ai-doctors",
      "title": "Clara (YC P26) is hiring a growth engineer to bring AI doctors to market",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/clara-2/jobs/8snci6k-founding-full-stack-growth-engineer\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49437566\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Founding full-stack growth Engineer$130K - $210K•0.10% - 0.40%•San Francisco, CA, USRoleEngineering, Full stackConnect directly with founders of the best YC-funded startups.Apply to role ›About the roleYou'll own Clara's growth engine, supporting our mission by helping more patients discover Clara and turn to it for their day-to-day primary care needs. Landing pages, onboarding funnel, experimentation, attribution, and lifecycle messaging all belong to you. You'll work across the entire funnel - from the first ad impression or search result, through signup and onboarding, into first chat, subscription and long-term retention. You'll write the code, ship the pages, wire the events, run the tests, and read the results yourself. You'll partner closely with our clinical and compliance teams to make sure every page, claim and experiment is medically accurate and HIPAA-safe.\nShip programmatic and SEO-driven page systems for condition, medication and geo intent\nIntegrate paid ad platforms with our attribution stack so every channel's true contribution is measurable\nBuild and iterate high-velocity landing pages and funnels in React + TypeScript\nOwn patient acquisition and onboarding end to end\nBuild in-product growth loops — activation nudges, referrals, sharing and re-engagement surfaces\nDesign onboarding that gets patients to first real value fast, then to habitual use\nDesign, build and launch experiments and MVPs autonomously — from hypothesis to shipped test to readout, without waiting to be told what to try\nTurn patient behavior signals into personalized in-product prompts, with clinical review in the loop\nOwn the experimentation platform end to end — assignment, exposure, guardrails, readouts\nInstrument the funnel in Amplitude and keep the event taxonomy trustworthy\nPartner with the clinical team to keep patients engaged with Clara over the long term and realize better health outcomes\nBuild event-triggered lifecycle journeys across onboarding rescue, reactivation and re-engagement\nOwn the CRM surfaces — email, SMS and in-product notifications — and the logic that decides who hears what, when\n3+ years software engineering, including 12+ months in a dedicated growth engineering role\nStrong full-stack ability — React + TypeScript front end, Python or TypeScript services\nExperience with product analytics instrumentation (Amplitude, Mixpanel or similar) and event taxonomy design\nExperience scoping and prioritizing initiatives using RICE or a similar framework, and defending the call\nMedical domain knowledge or healthcare AI experience\nComfortable using LLMs as a production tool for content, creative and internal tooling\nWhat Clara offers founding engineers\nShip code that affects real patient health outcomes\nMake architectural decisions for an AI-first medical practice\nWork directly with founders on technical strategy\nHigh-performance founding team at the forefront of healthcare AI\nIn-person collaboration in San Francisco (5 days/week)\nTalk to real patients and providers regularly\nGrowth stack: Amplitude (incl. session replay + Experiment), Customer.io, Stripe, Google/Meta/Reddit Ads APIs. Underneath: React 19 + TypeScript product app, Next.js + Payload CMS marketing site on Vercel, Python/Django backend on AWS, and frontier LLMs with proprietary prompts and tool calls.\nWe will sponsor TN, OPT and H1B transfer work permits for the right candidate.\nIntro call (30 min) - Meet founding team, learn about Clara's mission\nTechnical screen (60 min) - Domain-specific challenge\nOnsite (4 hours) - System design, code pairing, team fit\nAbout ClaraClara is an AI-powered medical practice on a bold mission: to add one billion years of healthspan to humanity. We are building the autonomous medical practice of the future, supervised by human medical providers who review and approve every medical decision.\nOur founders have built and scaled Circle Medical to over $100M in annual revenue, and founding executives have held key roles at Hims and Hers, GoodRx and Teladoc. We are full time in San Francisco and have raised $12M in pre-seed funding from Y Combinator and top investors. This is the A team, and we have a place for you.Founded:2025Batch:P26Team Size:9Status:ActiveLocation:San FranciscoFounders",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "gfavvas",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-25T17:28:52.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/logos/2eb543f912e3fbc3becf633f1826feed6c5cefe8.png?1764101930",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/clara-2/jobs/8snci6k-founding-full-stack-growth-engineer",
      "readTimeMinutes": 3,
      "language": "en"
