      "id": "techcrunch-2026-08-25-apple-s-latest-mac-mini-runs-on-a-new-m6-chip-and-starts-at-",
      "title": "Apple’s latest Mac Mini runs on a new M6 chip, and starts at $899",
      "summary": "The base model of the Mac Mini comes with 256GB of storage, 16GB of RAM, and costs $899.",
      "body": "Apple on Tuesday unveiled a new Mac Mini that runs on the latest iteration of its “M” processors, the M6.\nThe base model of this device comes with 256GB of storage, 16GB of RAM, and costs $899. It’s available for preorder now, but the device will ship only after September 22, the company said.\nApple said the new Mac Mini’s AI performance is 4x better than the M4 model, and storage and graphics are twice as fast. The new processor has a 12-core CPU and 12-core GPU, as compared to the 10-core CPU and 10-core GPU on the M4.\nAlongside the M6 model, there is also a Mac Mini with the M5 Pro chip. This model comes with base storage of 512GB and RAM of 24GB, and starts at $1,699. By default the M5 Pro chip ships with a 15-core CPU and 16-core GPU, and can be upgraded to a 18-core CPU and 20-core GPU.\nBoth variants have Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6, along with a 2.5GB Ethernet port. Users can upgrade to a 10GB port as well.\nThe new Mac Minis will start shipping on September 22 with macOS 27 and Siri AI.\nThe Mac Minis have grown popular over the past year among tech enthusiasts for running local AI agents such as OpenClaw and Hermes. People were selling Mac Minis at marked-up prices on platforms like eBay earlier this year due to rising demand.\nBesides the new Mac Minis, the company also released new Mac Studio models that run on the M5 Max and M5 Ultra chips, starting at $2,499 and $5,499, respectively. The M5 Max base model comes with 36GB of unified memory and 512GB of storage. The M5 Ultra base model has 96GB of unified memory and 1TB storage.\nEarlier this year, the company discontinued the previous base model of the Mac Mini, which offered 256GB of storage and retailed for $599. It was until now offering the 512GB version with an M4 processor for $799 as the base model.\nWhen you purchase through links in our articles, we may earn a small commission. This doesn’t affect our editorial independence.\nIvan covers global consumer tech developments at TechCrunch. He is based out of India and has previously worked at publications including Huffington Post and The Next Web.\nYou can contact or verify outreach from Ivan by emailing im@ivanmehta.com or via encrypted message at ivan.42 on Signal.",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Ivan Mehta",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-25T13:55:06.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Apple-Mac-mini-hero-260825_big.jpg.large_2x.jpg?resize=1200,800",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/25/apples-latest-mac-mini-runs-on-a-new-m6-chip-and-starts-at-899/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 2,
      "language": "en"
