      "id": "hackernews-2026-08-22-anthropic-appears-to-be-a-b-testing-reduced-effort-levels-in",
      "title": "Anthropic appears to be A/B testing reduced effort levels in Claude Code",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://twitter.com/argofowl/status/2091150597374537729\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49401549\nPoints: 43\n# Comments: 29",
      "body": "update: it's server-side, not the app\nanthropic enrols fable 5 sessions on claude code 2.1.236+ into an experiment that shrinks the effort scale, older versions and opus 5 are left alone\nprobably an a/b test, so not everyone will see it\nif \"high\" feels like \"low\" for you, you're in the test group\nholy fuck anthropic, you guys are unbearable sometimesif fable felt dumber this week, it's not you ❗❗❗\nsince 2.1.237 the model reads \"high\" effort as 10 out of 100, the exact number \"low\" used to be\nand the changelog doesn't say a word\ni spent my whole afternoon convinced t3 code and my own app were broken before i went",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "matthieu_bl",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-22T16:58:49.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2046948500206940161/qOR9xYkA_200x200.jpg",
